{"availability":"available","full":"b-tice/orbit_ui","name":"orbit_ui","description":"Orbit pedal assignment UI — concept demo (curves + spans editor, Ambient CSS night theme)","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-02T23:27:53Z","updated":"2026-10-12T19:29:47Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://b-tice.github.io/orbit_ui/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T00:51:51.201Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T00:51:51.201Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T00:51:51.201Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T02:10:25.306Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T00:51:51.201Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live at . The current version is shown in the page header (APPVERSION in orbit.js) and bumps with every feature addition.","A standalone web page that demos the Orbit pedal's Setup editor: setting response curves and zones for the pitch and yaw axes, and (v1.15) editing the Ground Control unit's Setups from a third tab. The MIDI and Analog Out tabs are not connected to a device — they are a UI concept for review, based on David Mash's reference/OrbitUIRough.jpeg and reference/AssignmentRough.jpeg sketches and the email thread of Aug–Sep 2026. The Ground Control tab speaks the unit's real bridge protocol, against a simulated unit in the page or a real one over WiFi / USB."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/b-tice/orbit_ui/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2fdc0902a89a567d965875a0625428c763c72a9464bb98bb39e2a562917abefc","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:25.457Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:25.457Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Live at . The current version is shown in the page header (APPVERSION in orbit.js) and bumps with every feature addition.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/b-tice/orbit_ui/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"2fdc0902a89a567d965